{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he fled.</b> From the room, lest the evil impulse overpower him." "<b>And he went outside.</b> Once he was outside the room, he walked slowly, without the movement of flight, so that they would not ask him: 'What is the matter with you that you flee, and who is pursuing you?' But she, when she saw that he had left the room in flight-movement, feared lest he do so outside the room as well and they ask him and he tell — therefore:"], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:57.975316411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}